{"name":"Hidden Valley","hex":"#689938","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hidden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["past participle of hide"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Located or positioned out of sight; not visually apparent.","Obscure. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hidden"},{"term":"valley","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elongated depression cast between hills or mountains, often with a river flowing through it.","An area which drains itself into a river."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form the shape of a valley."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/valley"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hidden Valley, Northern Territory","blocks":[{"text":"Hidden Valley is an eastern suburb in the city of Darwin, in the Northern Territory of Australia. It is the traditional country and waterways of the Larrakia people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Hidden_Valley_Raceway.jpg/330px-Hidden_Valley_Raceway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hidden_Valley%2C_Northern_Territory","wikidata":"Q5751977"},{"title":"Valley","blocks":[{"text":"A valley is an elongated low area often running between hills or mountains and typically containing a river or stream running from one end to the other. Most valleys are formed by erosion of the land surface by rivers or streams over a very long period. Some valleys are formed through erosion by glacial ice. These glaciers may remain present in valleys in high mountains or polar areas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Salta-VallesCalchaquies-P3140151.JPG/330px-Salta-VallesCalchaquies-P3140151.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley","wikidata":"Q39816"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimed